    "q-82286": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82286",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=(-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=-\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
