    "q-82285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82285",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn. \n\n- The matrix $A$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
