    "q-140047": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140047",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find $det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|B|=-1\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-2det(B)=0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
