    "q-43058": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43058",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}|.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 4=-40\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
